  "rules": [
    "When sentiment history shows a recent spike (0.67 or 1.0) followed by zero sentiment, the model significantly overestimates price recovery; apply a downward correction of 5-8 EUR to counteract the 'overshoot' bias.",
    "The model exhibits strong mean reversion lag, assuming prices will slowly climb back to historical averages after sharp drops, whereas true outcomes often continue falling or stabilize at new lows for extended periods.",
    "In high-volatility regimes (price swings >5 EUR), the model's linear projection fails to capture the 'mean-reverting' nature of carbon markets, resulting in consistent upward bias during correction phases.",
    "Sentiment spikes preceding a 30-day horizon forecast are unreliable predictors of immediate price action; true outcomes often ignore sentiment momentum and revert to volatility-weighted averages."
  ]
